id: pm-todos-iw4m
title: A truncated list-all answer is consumed as if it were the whole workspace
description: "Both list-all readers take .items and act on it as if it were everything. readPmItemsForUpsert builds the upsert key index, and fetchPmItems feeds the TODO export. Neither consults the completeness receipt the envelope has carried since 2026.8.15. Under pm-cli 2026.8.14 the same calls returned 10 items of a 682-item workspace with truncated true, so the upsert index missed keys and created duplicates while the exporter wrote a TODO file missing 98 percent of its rows, both reporting success. Two aggravating factors found alongside it: readPmItemsForUpsert passed a hardcoded limit of 10000 rows, which with a completeness gate in place converts every larger workspace from a big read into a hard refusal of upsert, and fetchPmItems passed no maxBuffer at all, so an overrun kills the child with a null status and empty stderr and surfaces as an unattributable pm list-all failed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: completeness,pm-cli
created_at: "2026-08-15T12:01:01.678Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T12:18:33.402Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T12:01:12.090Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T12:01:12.090Z"
author: codex
resolution: "assertListAllComplete refuses an envelope carrying any of truncated, has_more, a completeness.status other than complete (an absent receipt included), or omission_receipt.has_omissions, naming the tripped signal, the count-versus-total scale, and which operation was refused. Both readers call it. The hardcoded limit of 10000 is removed from the upsert read and fetchPmItems now passes a maxBuffer and classifies the ENOBUFS case. The CLI is exact-pinned at 2026.8.15 with a >=2026.8.15 peer floor."
expected_result: "A truncated or degraded envelope aborts the upsert or the export with a message naming the signal, instead of building a key index that creates duplicates or writing a TODO file missing most of its rows."
actual_result: "153 of 153 tests pass, up from 146. Neutering assertListAllComplete fails 5 of them. The seven new cases are driven from a real 2026.8.15 envelope captured from the CLI against a live two-item workspace with exactly one field mutated per case, including the bare-array case that carries no receipt and must not be refused."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T12:18:33.402Z",pi-agent,"Review round two on PR 52. Three findings, all correct, two of them defects introduced by round one.\n\nGreptile P2 and CodeRabbit both spotted that assertListAllComplete ran INSIDE the parse try/catch in the upsert reader. That bare catch replaced the CommandError with 'Could not parse pm list-all --json output', so an incomplete-envelope refusal reached the operator as a parse error with the signal name and the count-versus-total scale stripped out. The gate still refused, but the diagnostic it exists to produce was destroyed. The parse is now its own try/catch and the gate runs after it.\n\nCodeRabbit Major: a bare array passes the gate by design, since it carries no receipt to contradict, but the export reader then did parsed.items on an array, resolved undefined, and exported an EMPTY todo file reporting success. That is the exact silent-partial failure this change exists to remove, reintroduced one line below the gate that prevents it. Both readers now go through a shared readItemsFromListAll that handles the envelope, results and bare-array shapes and refuses a non-array items field.\n\nThe first regression test I wrote for that re-implemented the shape logic inline instead of calling the function, which proves only that the test agrees with itself. Replaced with assertions against the real exported helper.\n\nReviewers also flagged that manifest.json and package.json make the same compatibility claim to two different installers, npm and the pm host, with nothing binding them. This package had no pm_min_version at all while its peer floor said 2026.8.15. Added, and a test now asserts the two are equal; injecting 2026.7.28 fails it.\n\n157 of 157 tests pass, release:check exit 0."
close_reason: "assertListAllComplete refuses an envelope carrying any of truncated, has_more, a completeness.status other than complete (an absent receipt included), or omission_receipt.has_omissions, naming the tripped signal, the count-versus-total scale, and which operation was refused. Both readers call it. The hardcoded limit of 10000 is removed from the upsert read and fetchPmItems now passes a maxBuffer and classifies the ENOBUFS case. The CLI is exact-pinned at 2026.8.15 with a >=2026.8.15 peer floor."
body: ""
